  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "This release upgrades to NTokenizers 7.0.1 and reworks the Markdown renderer from a buffer-then-display model into a fully forward-only, per-token streaming pipeline, with a number of parsing and rendering fixes.\n\n## Markdown streaming (rewrite)\n\n- Markdown is now rendered forward-only: each token is written to the console as it arrives, the left side (borders, gutters, markers) is composed from the active nesting frame stack, and lines wrap only when a token no longer fits. The previous buffer-then-render LiveBlock model is gone.\n- Nested Markdown (blockquote, heading, list items) is streamed token by token; list-item content can contain nested blocks such as quotes and lists.\n- Root paragraphs are written directly and verbatim, so soft breaks inside a paragraph are preserved.\n- Nested HTML style/script content is tokenized and streamed inline without the previous per-element handler delay.\n- Nested list indentation and frame ordering are corrected.\n- A pending block separator no longer renders as a blank line before a list's nested list.\n- Console width is cached with a redirected-output fallback (80), removing the WindowWidth IOException when stdout is redirected.\n- The unused generic Heading style property was removed; headings render through MarkdownHeadingStyles.\n\n## Tables\n\n- Tables render in a Spectre live region that grows and refreshes as rows arrive, restoring the previous growing-table behavior on the new streaming path.\n\n## Writers\n\n- The Emoji writer now supports the `:rocket:` short-code syntax.\n- The Link writer rendering was improved.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Upgraded to NTokenizers 7.0.",
